  "question": {
    "text": "A given ideal gas with $\\gamma=\\frac{C_p}{C_v}=1.5$ at a temperature $T$. If the gas is compressed adiabatically to one-fourth of its initial volume, the final temperature will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4Z4iv",
      "text": "\n$2 \\sqrt{2} T$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1TZjT",
      "text": "\n$4 T$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4LhI4",
      "text": "\n$2 T$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "hfn49",
      "text": "\n$8 T$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$T V^{\\gamma-1}=$ constant\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& T_1 V_1^{\\gamma-1}=\\mathrm{T}_2 V_2^{\\gamma-1} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow T(V)^{1 / 2}=\\mathrm{T}_2\\left(\\frac{V}{4}\\right)^{1 / 2} \\\\\n& {\\left[\\because \\gamma=1.5, T_1=T, V_1=V \\text { and } V_2=\\frac{V}{4}\\right]} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad T_2=\\left(\\frac{4 V}{V}\\right)^{1 / 2} T=2 T\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
